{"ld": 1266, "paper": "HP841", "session": "132", "title": "Resolve, Directing the Department of Health and Human Services, Office of Behavioral Health to Convene a Working Group to Propose a Plan for Expanding the Reach of Treatment Courts (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "h-hasenfus-tavis", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-lee-adam", "h-milliken-nina", "h-sinclair-david", "s-talbot-ross-rachel"], "committee_code": "JUD", "committee_name": "Judiciary", "summary": {"text": "This resolve requires the Attorney General to establish a working group comprised of a multidisciplinary group of stakeholders to develop a plan for expanding the availability of adult drug treatment courts, family treatment courts and veterans treatment courts across the State by ensuring that defendants in each prosecutorial district and county have access to these specialty court dockets. The Attorney General is required to submit a report, including any recommendations from the working group, to the Joint Standing Committee on Judiciary no later than January 1, 2026. The committee may report out legislation related to the report to the Second Regular Session of the 132nd Legislature.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0841&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Finally Passed", "final_disposition": {"label": "Finally Passed", "date": "2025-06-20", "governor_action": "Signed", "governor_action_date": "2025-06-20"}, "fiscal_status": "Fiscal Impact", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1266)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0841&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-721)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0841&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}], "amendments": [{"id": "C-A (H-721)", "description": null, "sponsor": null, "status": "Adopted by House & Senate", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0841&item=